course: dictionary
lesson: 2672
title: Diagonally: corner to corner
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you the direction something goes. Diagonally is one of them. Picture a square: a line from one corner straight to the opposite corner is a diagonal line.
explain: Diagonally can also mean at a slant, not straight up and down or straight across. «You walk straight across the road, never run, and never cross diagonally, on a slant, which keeps you in the road longer.» The word straight is the clue: the safe way is straight across, and diagonally is the slanting way.
explain: Ask yourself: does the line go straight across, or does it slant from one corner to the opposite one? If it slants, it is diagonal. Try the meaning in the sentence: «never cross on a slant» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Diagonally means in a straight slanting line from one corner to the opposite corner.
fact: Diagonally can also mean at a slant, not straight up and down or straight across.
fact: A square cut diagonally makes two triangles.
fact: «Diagonally opposite» tells you where something is: the corner across from you, not the one next to you.
fact: Bishops in chess move diagonally.
exercise: «You walk straight across the road, never run.» Which way does the sentence say is safe to cross? | Along the pavement, then back | *Straight across | Diagonally, on a slant | Running as fast as you can
exercise: Mia cuts a square piece of paper from one corner to the opposite corner. How does she cut it? | In a wiggly circle | Along one edge | *Diagonally | Up and down only
exercise: In the room, the cupboard is diagonally opposite the door. Where is the cupboard? | *In the corner across from the door | Under the door | Right next to the door | Outside the room
test: Mum says, «Cut the cake diagonally.» What does diagonally mean here? | Into tiny crumbs | Straight down the middle, side to side | *On a slant, from one corner to the opposite corner | Round the outside edge
test: Which way does a chess bishop move? | Straight forward only | *Diagonally | In a circle | Sideways only
exam: «You walk straight across the road, never run, and never cross diagonally, on a slant.» Why does the author say never cross diagonally? | Because it is only a rule for cars | Because it is faster | Because diagonal is a colour | *Because a slant keeps you in the road longer, which is less safe
